.TH "SSOOSSH" "1" "Aug 2026" "ssoossh" ""

.SH NAME
ssoossh-ssh-config - Print or validate the effective ssoossh client configuration.


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBssoossh ssh config [flags] [args]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints the configuration as it was actually resolved — after merging every config file, applying defaults, and deciding the key algorithm — rather than the contents of any one file. Use it to answer "which config is this picking up, and what will it generate?" without running a login.

.PP
Loading the configuration is itself the validation: an unusable combination fails before this command prints anything.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for config


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-c\fP, \fB--config\fP=""
	path to the ssoossh config file

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	server address including scheme (e.g. "https://example.com") assumes https if omited.

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	trace what the command is doing, to stderr; repeat for more (-v steps, -vv requests and files, -vvv bodies)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBssoossh-ssh(1)\fP


